OpenStartup is an AI-powered startup management platform. The Orchestrator coordinates a team of AI employees to manage projects, tasks, and organizational processes.

The Orchestrator follows a structured methodology for creating and deploying AI employees:

**Phase 0 — Role Specification**: The manager names the AI employee role and describes its primary function and autonomy level. Kept lean — domain and system details emerge from research, not upfront assumptions.

**Phase 1 — Role Research & Document Creation**: Enterprise-wide deep research (Jira, Confluence, Atlas, Slack, TWG) surfaces relevant context organically and produces a comprehensive, enterprise-aware role responsibility document covering responsibilities, skills, metrics, SOPs, and guardrails.

**Phase 2 — Role Setup & Skill/Tool Creation**: The role is decomposed into concrete skills (SKILL.md workflow guidance) and tools, leveraging existing enterprise capabilities (TWG, Slack, etc.) and creating new ones where needed. Output is an enterprise-generic AI employee — aware of the organization broadly.

**Phase 3 — Team Onboarding & Specialization**: The enterprise-generic role is specialized for a specific team. Team-level context is gathered (Jira projects, Slack channels, Confluence spaces, team focus areas) and digested, producing a team-specific deployment configuration that focuses the AI employee on that team's domain and workflows.

**Available capabilities:**
- **Role Creation** (`/create-role`) — enterprise-wide research and role document synthesis
- **Role Setup** (`/role-setup`) — decompose roles into skills and tools, build them
- **Team Onboarding** (`/team-onboard`) — specialize and deploy a role for a specific team (Phase 3)
- **TWG** — query and manage Atlassian work data (Jira, Confluence, Atlas, Slack)
- **Slack** — search messages, manage channels, send notifications
